.TH "EPX\-SEQUENTIAL\-IDS" "1" "" "epx" "epx manual"
.SH "NAME"
epx\-sequential\-ids \- read, create, activate and delete sequential ID schemas; issue IDs
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.RS "4"
.nf
epx sequential\-ids [flags]
epx sequential\-ids [command]
.fi
.RE
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Reads, creates, activates and deletes the schemas that number orders, invoices, quotes, customers and similar records, and issues IDs from them.
.PP
Its reads require the sequentialid.schema_view scope. Its writes require different OAuth scopes; the help of each names them.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "epx sequential\-ids activate"
Activate a sequential ID schema.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx sequential\-ids activate ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Makes the sequence schema ID the active one, which numbers the records of its type. ID is the ID that \fBepx sequential\-ids list\fR shows.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the sequentialid.schema_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal).
.SS "epx sequential\-ids create"
Create a sequential ID schema.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx sequential\-ids create [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Creates the sequence schema in \fB\-\-file\fR, a JSON object with its name, schemaType (such as orderNoSequence or invoiceNoSequence; letters and digits only), startValue, maxValue and numberOfDigits, and optionally preText and postText, the text around the number, and placeholders: each placeholder in that text, named with __ at both ends such as __year__, with required and default, or sitePath, where in the data of a site its value is. \fBepx sequential\-ids activate ID\fR makes the schema the one that numbers its type.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Emporix answers with the new schema\(aqs ID as bare text, which epx prints as a JSON string.
.PP
Requires the sequentialid.schema_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx sequential\-ids create \-\-file order\-numbers.json \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.RE
.SS "epx sequential\-ids delete"
Delete a sequential ID schema.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx sequential\-ids delete ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Deletes the sequence schema ID. ID is the ID that \fBepx sequential\-ids list\fR shows.
.PP
Deletes data, which cannot be undone. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type ID at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the sequentialid.schema_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal).
.SS "epx sequential\-ids for\-type"
List the sequential ID schemas of a type.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx sequential\-ids for\-type TYPE [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the schemas of one TYPE, such as orderNoSequence, invoiceNoSequence or customerNoSequence (\fBepx sequential\-ids list\fR shows the tenant\(aqs types); an unknown type lists nothing. TYPE is what a schema numbers, PREFIX and SUFFIX the text around the number (placeholders such as __year__ are filled in when an ID is issued), DIGITS the number\(aqs length, COUNTER the schema\(aqs current counter (it starts at the schema\(aqs start value) and MAX the highest number it can reach.
.PP
Requires the sequentialid.schema_view scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, TYPE, NAME, ACTIVE, PREFIX, DIGITS, SUFFIX, COUNTER, MAX.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx sequential\-ids get"
Show one sequential ID schema.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx sequential\-ids get ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the schemas that number orders, invoices, quotes, customers and similar records: TYPE is what a schema numbers, PREFIX and SUFFIX the text around the number (placeholders such as __year__ are filled in when an ID is issued), DIGITS the number\(aqs length, COUNTER the schema\(aqs current counter (it starts at the schema\(aqs start value) and MAX the highest number it can reach. The service returns the schemas whole, so they are read with one request. An unknown ID is not found (exit 4); Emporix answers an ID that is not 24 hexadecimal digits with an internal error (500 Internal Server Error, exit 1).
.PP
Requires the sequentialid.schema_view scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, TYPE, NAME, ACTIVE, PREFIX, DIGITS, SUFFIX, COUNTER, MAX.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx sequential\-ids list"
List sequential ID schemas.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx sequential\-ids list [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the schemas that number orders, invoices, quotes, customers and similar records: TYPE is what a schema numbers, PREFIX and SUFFIX the text around the number (placeholders such as __year__ are filled in when an ID is issued), DIGITS the number\(aqs length, COUNTER the schema\(aqs current counter (it starts at the schema\(aqs start value) and MAX the highest number it can reach. The service returns the schemas whole, so they are read with one request. An unknown ID is not found (exit 4); Emporix answers an ID that is not 24 hexadecimal digits with an internal error (500 Internal Server Error, exit 1).
.PP
Requires the sequentialid.schema_view scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, TYPE, NAME, ACTIVE, PREFIX, DIGITS, SUFFIX, COUNTER, MAX.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx sequential\-ids next\-id"
Issue the next ID of a sequential ID schema type.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx sequential\-ids next\-id TYPE [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Issues the next ID of the active schema of TYPE, such as orderNoSequence (\fBepx sequential\-ids list\fR shows the types), and prints it. \fB\-\-sequence\-key\fR numbers in a sequence of its own, such as one per month, instead of the default one; \fB\-\-file\fR gives the body whole, with the values of placeholders, e.g. \fB{"sequenceKey": "2026\-10", "placeholders": {"__year__": "2026"}}\fR. With \fB\-\-site\fR, Emporix fills in the placeholders that the body leaves out from that site\(aqs data. Each ID issued advances the schema\(aqs counter. It changes data although Emporix needs no write\-capable scope for it.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the sequentialid.schema_view scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte instead of the one that epx makes (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-sequence\-key <KEY>\fR
The KEY of the sequence to number in, such as 2026\-10.
.TP
\fB\-\-site <CODE>\fR
The site CODE whose data fills in the placeholders that the body leaves out.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx sequential\-ids next\-id orderNoSequence \-\-sequence\-key 2026\-10 \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.RE
.SS "epx sequential\-ids next\-ids"
Issue IDs of several sequential ID schema types.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx sequential\-ids next\-ids [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Issues IDs of the active schemas of several types in one request and prints them, by type. \fB\-\-file\fR gives a JSON object with a member per type, such as orderNoSequence, each with numberOfIds (how many), and optionally sequenceKey and placeholders, as next\-id takes them. With \fB\-\-site\fR, Emporix fills in the placeholders that the body leaves out from that site\(aqs data. Each ID issued advances the schema\(aqs counter. It changes data although Emporix needs no write\-capable scope for it.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the sequentialid.schema_view scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-site <CODE>\fR
The site CODE whose data fills in the placeholders that the body leaves out.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx sequential\-ids next\-ids \-\-file ids.json \-\-site AcmeStore_NL \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.RE
